\DOC PURE_BOUNDER_TAC

\TYPE {PURE_BOUNDER_TAC : thm list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves a real-arithmetic inequality goal outright from bounding facts supplied
as theorems, closing the goal.

\DESCRIBE
Takes one argument of type {thm list}: theorems giving ranges and defining
equations for the real-valued subterms appearing in the goal's conclusion,
which supply the bounds used to discharge the goal. Applied to a goal whose
conclusion is an inequality between real-valued arithmetic expressions, or a
conjunction of such inequalities, it closes the goal:
{
   A ?- t
   ======================  PURE_BOUNDER_TAC thl
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces only this single outcome occurs — goals closed — and
only with conclusions that are strict or non-strict real inequalities built
from arithmetic over terms constrained by the supplied theorems; the goals
carry large assumption lists {A}, which are left untouched, with nothing added
to them.

\ENDDOC
